From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: At30c <173511395+At30c@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:20:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: exynos9611: M21: restore the stock Mali r32p1 DDK

The Android 17 target retains the SM-F415F/M21s vendor graphics stack.
Its libGLES_mali.so identifies itself as MaliG72 r32p1-01bet2, while the
universal9611 kernel currently selects r38p1 for every device.  Those DDKs
do not share a stable userspace/kernel ioctl ABI: EGL cannot create a base
context, SurfaceFlinger aborts, and init eventually enters Rescue Party.

The universal-kernel change which selected r38p1 for all devices replaced
the original M21 r32p1 selection.  Restore r32p1 only for the M21 target;
do not change the other device defconfigs or any Android 17 compatibility
backports.

---
 arch/arm64/configs/exynos9611-m21_defconfig | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/exynos9611-m21_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/exynos9611-m21_defconfig
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/exynos9611-m21_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/exynos9611-m21_defconfig
@@ -3055,8 +3055,8 @@ CONFIG_MALI_DDK_VERSION=y
 # CONFIG_MALI_BIFROST_R19P0_Q is not set
 # CONFIG_MALI_BIFROST_R25P1_R is not set
 # CONFIG_MALI_BIFROST_R26P0_R is not set
-# CONFIG_MALI_BIFROST_R32P1 is not set
-CONFIG_MALI_BIFROST_R38P1=y
+CONFIG_MALI_BIFROST_R32P1=y
+# CONFIG_MALI_BIFROST_R38P1 is not set
 CONFIG_MALI_MIDGARD=y
 CONFIG_MALI_GATOR_SUPPORT=y
 # CONFIG_MALI_MIDGARD_DVFS is not set
-- 
